WEBVTT

00:00:01.355 --> 00:00:02.955
EBAY ELAYNE:
So, we are set to ship

00:00:03.035 --> 00:00:04.475
one Sugar Rush
steering wheel...

00:00:04.635 --> 00:00:05.995
-RALPH: Mmm-hmm.
-...to a Litwak's Family

00:00:06.075 --> 00:00:07.515
FunLand in Los Aburridos,
California.

00:00:07.595 --> 00:00:08.595
Yep!

00:00:08.675 --> 00:00:09.755
With expedited shipping,

00:00:09.835 --> 00:00:11.755
that should arrive
Wednesday morning.

00:00:11.915 --> 00:00:14.435
That's two whole days before
Litwak scraps your game.

00:00:14.595 --> 00:00:16.315
We're way ahead of schedule.

00:00:16.475 --> 00:00:17.515
We rule!

00:00:17.675 --> 00:00:19.355
I'll just need
a credit card number.

00:00:19.715 --> 00:00:21.475
Sorry, what's a
credit card number?

00:00:21.635 --> 00:00:23.715
A credit card number.

00:00:23.875 --> 00:00:26.315
Number. Right.
Uh, seven.

00:00:26.715 --> 00:00:27.915
Excuse me?

00:00:28.115 --> 00:00:30.995
Sorry, no. You're right,
ridiculous. I meant 11.

00:00:31.155 --> 00:00:32.795
Those aren't
credit card numbers.

00:00:32.955 --> 00:00:34.275
I'm pretty sure they are.

00:00:34.435 --> 00:00:36.195
How exactly do you intend
to pay for this item, sir?

00:00:36.355 --> 00:00:38.635
You owe $27,001.

00:00:38.795 --> 00:00:39.795
What?

00:00:39.955 --> 00:00:42.195
Dollars? Dollars like money?

00:00:42.355 --> 00:00:45.235
Yes, and if you don't
have a credit card...

00:00:45.395 --> 00:00:47.235
we also accept PayPal,
Venmo,

00:00:47.315 --> 00:00:49.275
ProPay, SquareCash
and BuzzzyBucks.

00:00:49.355 --> 00:00:50.795
-Uh...
-(CHUCKLING)

00:00:50.875 --> 00:00:52.875
You're gonna laugh. Okay.

00:00:54.635 --> 00:00:58.315
So this big galoot,
he left his wallet at home.

00:00:58.475 --> 00:01:01.035
Yeah, yeah, I did leave
my wallet at home,

00:01:01.115 --> 00:01:03.195
in my wallet room.
And the door's locked.

00:01:03.595 --> 00:01:04.835
Uh-huh.

00:01:04.915 --> 00:01:07.075
Look. If you don't pay
within 24 hours...

00:01:07.235 --> 00:01:09.235
you will be in violation
of the unpaid item policy...

00:01:09.395 --> 00:01:11.915
you will forfeit the bid,
and you will lose this item.

00:01:12.075 --> 00:01:13.075
Next!

00:01:15.155 --> 00:01:16.395
Hey, buddy, you going to eboy?

00:01:16.555 --> 00:01:18.715
Well, I got some free advice
for you. Don't.

00:01:18.875 --> 00:01:20.275
What a scam!

00:01:20.435 --> 00:01:23.635
(GRUNTING) We were so close,
and we would have gotten...

00:01:24.555 --> 00:01:26.555
Look, their signs
aren't even real!

00:01:26.635 --> 00:01:28.075
(SHOUTS)

00:01:31.795 --> 00:01:34.395
What the heck? Dang Internet.

00:01:34.475 --> 00:01:35.595
(CHIMING)

00:01:35.675 --> 00:01:37.635
(SHOUTING)

00:01:37.715 --> 00:01:40.715
Oh, man, oh, man, oh, man.

00:01:40.875 --> 00:01:42.875
Hey, kid. What's going on?
What's wrong?

00:01:43.035 --> 00:01:44.355
If I don't have
a steering wheel,

00:01:44.435 --> 00:01:46.275
I don't have a game,
I'm gameless.

00:01:46.435 --> 00:01:49.235
There's only one steering
wheel in the whole Internet...

00:01:49.395 --> 00:01:52.235
and we blew our chance
to get it. We blew it!

00:01:52.395 --> 00:01:54.195
Hey, hey, hey, calm down.

00:01:54.355 --> 00:01:55.835
We came here
to save your game,

00:01:55.915 --> 00:01:57.115
and that's what
we're gonna do.

00:01:57.195 --> 00:01:58.195
Right.

00:01:58.275 --> 00:01:59.755
-Okay?
-Okay, yeah.

00:01:59.835 --> 00:02:01.035
(EXHALES)

00:02:01.115 --> 00:02:02.155
There you go.

00:02:02.875 --> 00:02:04.915
Now look, all we got to do...

00:02:05.075 --> 00:02:07.995
is figure out a way
to earn a little bit of moola.

00:02:08.155 --> 00:02:11.635
We're video game characters,
Ralph. We don't have moola.

00:02:11.795 --> 00:02:13.435
Unless you can think
of some magical way

00:02:13.515 --> 00:02:16.315
to get rich
playing video games.

00:02:17.875 --> 00:02:18.955
(BOTH GASP)

00:02:19.595 --> 00:02:21.395
Wanna get rich
playing video games?

00:02:21.555 --> 00:02:23.235
Click right here
to find out how.

00:02:23.395 --> 00:02:25.395
-Back off, pop-up!
-(GROANING)

00:02:25.475 --> 00:02:26.555
POP-UP BLOCKER:
Right this way, miss.

00:02:26.715 --> 00:02:28.275
Dang pop-up blockers.

00:02:28.435 --> 00:02:30.395
Why does everybody
gotta be so mean?

00:02:30.555 --> 00:02:32.755
Ooh! There he is! Oh, thank
goodness you're still here!

00:02:32.955 --> 00:02:36.155
Me and my friend here, we got
24 hours to make $27,001...

00:02:36.315 --> 00:02:37.475
or she loses her game.

00:02:37.635 --> 00:02:38.715
Yeah, can you please tell us

00:02:38.835 --> 00:02:40.835
how to get rich
playing video games?

00:02:40.915 --> 00:02:42.155
(STAMMERING)
You bet! (CHUCKLES)

00:02:42.835 --> 00:02:45.155
Come on, click here, and
I'll take you to my website.

00:02:45.235 --> 00:02:46.835
(RALPH EXCLAIMING)

00:02:47.435 --> 00:02:48.555
(RALPH GROANS)

00:02:48.635 --> 00:02:51.155
You got an ample carriage
there, buster. (CHUCKLES)

00:02:51.315 --> 00:02:52.395
Causing a little drag.

00:02:52.595 --> 00:02:53.915
Sorry. You're getting close
to the edge.

00:02:53.995 --> 00:02:54.995
Huh?

00:02:55.075 --> 00:02:57.635
RALPH: You see the...?
The edge. The edge! (SHOUTS)

00:02:57.835 --> 00:02:59.715
(ENGINE SPUTTERING)

00:02:59.795 --> 00:03:02.435
SPAMLEY: By the way,
my name is JP Spamley...

00:03:02.595 --> 00:03:04.035
and I'd like to welcome
the both of you

00:03:04.155 --> 00:03:05.595
to the Spamley family.

00:03:05.675 --> 00:03:06.715
(SPAMLEY CHUCKLES)

00:03:07.475 --> 00:03:10.315
All right,
step into my parlor.

00:03:10.475 --> 00:03:12.475
This is your website?

00:03:12.635 --> 00:03:13.915
I know what you're thinking,
not to worry.

00:03:14.115 --> 00:03:15.675
My anti-virus guy
was just here.

00:03:15.835 --> 00:03:17.155
-Clean as a...
-(RAT SQUEAKING)

00:03:17.235 --> 00:03:18.555
Oh! (GRUNTING)

00:03:18.635 --> 00:03:19.635
Dang it!

00:03:19.755 --> 00:03:20.955
Oh, my gosh.
That's embarrassing.

00:03:21.035 --> 00:03:22.835
(CHUCKLES) Anyway,
I know it's a bit of a mess...

00:03:22.915 --> 00:03:23.915
Hey, Gord!

00:03:24.075 --> 00:03:25.715
But I do have a system here,
I really do.

00:03:25.875 --> 00:03:27.795
If I can just find that...
Gord!

00:03:27.955 --> 00:03:30.235
-I just got to find this list.
-(BOTH SHRIEK)

00:03:30.315 --> 00:03:31.315
SPAMLEY: Oh, there you are.

00:03:31.515 --> 00:03:34.075
These guys are looking to get
rich playing video games.

00:03:34.595 --> 00:03:35.955
What do you got for them,
partner?

00:03:45.035 --> 00:03:46.155
Thank you.

00:03:46.715 --> 00:03:50.195
"Fishwife's amulet,
Wizard Quest, three dollars."

00:03:50.355 --> 00:03:54.075
"Foxhole hammer, Zombie
Crusades, five dollars"?

00:03:54.235 --> 00:03:55.475
Now, those there are

00:03:55.555 --> 00:03:57.835
some of your more commonplace,
low-dollar items.

00:03:58.035 --> 00:04:00.155
Can you back up a sec,
Mr. Spamley?

00:04:00.235 --> 00:04:02.395
Um, you're saying if we find

00:04:02.475 --> 00:04:05.475
the Golden Cleats
from Pro League Soccer...

00:04:05.675 --> 00:04:08.155
we find those and bring them
back here to you...

00:04:08.315 --> 00:04:11.675
then a human being in the
real world will pay us $15?

00:04:11.835 --> 00:04:12.875
Yes, ma'am.

00:04:12.955 --> 00:04:15.235
Welcome to the exciting world
of loot hunting.

00:04:15.435 --> 00:04:16.515
Folks go into games...

00:04:16.675 --> 00:04:18.515
they harvest
the most coveted items...

00:04:18.675 --> 00:04:20.235
and they sell them
on my website

00:04:20.315 --> 00:04:22.515
to the highest bidder. Ha-ha?

00:04:22.595 --> 00:04:23.915
Okay, but here's the thing...

00:04:24.075 --> 00:04:25.955
we need like
a buttload of money.

00:04:26.155 --> 00:04:28.955
So, do you have any more
lucrative items, maybe?

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:30.435
Gord!

00:04:31.035 --> 00:04:32.355
-Gord!
-(BOTH SHRIEK)

00:04:32.435 --> 00:04:33.515
Oh, there you are.

00:04:35.755 --> 00:04:37.715
Thank you, buddy.
You're such a nice guy.

00:04:37.995 --> 00:04:40.515
Is $40,000 lucrative
enough for you?

00:04:40.595 --> 00:04:41.595
-Whoa!
-Whoa.

00:04:41.675 --> 00:04:42.995
It's more than enough.

00:04:43.155 --> 00:04:44.955
I got a guy
in Des Moines, Iowa...

00:04:45.115 --> 00:04:47.835
who will pay 40 grand
for Shank's car...

00:04:47.995 --> 00:04:49.955
from a game
called Slaughter Race.

00:04:50.115 --> 00:04:51.115
A racing game?

00:04:51.275 --> 00:04:53.355
That's right. Slaughter Race
is the most popular

00:04:53.435 --> 00:04:55.075
online racing game out there.

00:04:55.235 --> 00:04:57.195
However,
it is wicked dangerous.

00:04:57.355 --> 00:04:58.635
We ain't afraid of danger.

00:04:58.795 --> 00:05:00.635
This kid's the best racer
in the whole world.

00:05:00.795 --> 00:05:03.155
We'll get you that car,
no problemo.

00:05:03.635 --> 00:05:07.195
ANNOUNCER: Slaughter Race!
Enter at your own risk.

00:05:07.315 --> 00:05:08.555
(TIRES SCREECHING)

00:05:11.995 --> 00:05:13.435
(HORN BLARING)

00:05:13.515 --> 00:05:16.875
Okay, this game
is kind of amazing.

00:05:18.435 --> 00:05:21.435
Meh, the attention to detail
is pretty impressive.

00:05:21.515 --> 00:05:22.515
(COUGHING)

00:05:22.595 --> 00:05:24.315
I don't think
I've ever been in a game

00:05:24.395 --> 00:05:25.755
-with smog before.
-(BOTH GASP)

00:05:25.875 --> 00:05:27.035
-(DOG BARKING)
-(RALPH SHOUTING)

00:05:27.115 --> 00:05:29.555
-Nice kitty. Nice kitty.
-Easy, boy. Easy.

00:05:29.995 --> 00:05:31.155
(RALPH AND VANELLOPE SHRIEK)

00:05:32.155 --> 00:05:33.395
(WATER SPLASHES)

00:05:33.475 --> 00:05:35.795
Let's just find Shank's car
and get outta here.

00:05:35.955 --> 00:05:36.955
Agreed.

00:05:42.755 --> 00:05:43.995
-Look. Look.
-Whoa!

00:05:44.075 --> 00:05:45.075
RALPH: There it is.

00:05:45.275 --> 00:05:47.115
VANELLOPE:
That car is gorgeous.

00:05:47.315 --> 00:05:49.395
No wonder it's worth so much.

00:05:49.475 --> 00:05:50.555
-(SHUSHES)
-(FOOTSTEPS)

00:05:50.635 --> 00:05:52.635
RALPH: Aw, sugar.

00:05:52.795 --> 00:05:55.035
-Players. They beat us to it.
-Aw.

00:05:55.235 --> 00:05:57.435
JIMMY: 31 hours
of continuous gameplay...

00:05:57.595 --> 00:06:00.195
and we've finally
found Shank's car.

00:06:00.355 --> 00:06:01.915
Let's jack this ride.

00:06:02.075 --> 00:06:04.275
Oh, yeah, DirtySocks,
it's on.

00:06:04.475 --> 00:06:06.115
JIMMY'S GRANDMA: Jim! Jimmy?

00:06:06.275 --> 00:06:09.115
You're not playing that
horrible game again, are you?

00:06:09.195 --> 00:06:10.515
-(LAUGHS)
-No, Grandma!

00:06:10.595 --> 00:06:11.795
I'm doing my homework.

00:06:11.955 --> 00:06:13.315
Okay, like I said...

00:06:13.475 --> 00:06:15.115
Let's jack this ride.

00:06:15.755 --> 00:06:17.035
(TIFFANY WHIMPERS)

00:06:21.155 --> 00:06:22.795
SHANK: Well, well, well.

00:06:23.995 --> 00:06:27.795
While the cat was away,
these mice tried to play.

